@isabella_m_weber explains why inflation and rising inequality go hand-in-hand: when there are price shocks for life’s essentials that boost corporate profits, this is a mechanism for wealth redistribution from the working class to the ultra-rich.

in the latest @betterfuturepod episode, we discuss economic policies that would reorient our priorities away from endless profits for the rich, and toward dignified livelihoods for all working people. the conversation is full of detail — comment “ep” and i’ll send it to you.

the discussion is based around Dr. Weber’s new book, Anti-Fascist Economic

@isabella_m_weber explains why fascism and neoliberalism are natural siblings: they are both willing to treat parts of society as collateral damage. in the latest @betterfuturepod episode, we discuss what it would take to build an anti-fascist economy instead. comment “ep” and we’ll send you the full convo, which is full of specific economic policy ideas.

